    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you on the \"global trend\" part, but i'm seeing a lot of reports about the massive problems with grid stability and the fact that we don't even have enough lithium or cobalt to actually make this happen on the scale people are talking about. it feels like some of these \"inevitable\" predictions ignore the actual physics and supply chain realities. wouldn't it be a bit reckless to assume this is a settled matter given how much volatility the transition itself is going to create in the markets?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
